<section class="paper">
  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ The strategy</span>
      <h2>The hardest part of college is deciding to <span class="serif">start.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <p>Idaho has one of the lowest go-on rates in the country. In 2024 just 43.6% of high-school graduates enrolled the next fall, well under the state's 60% goal.</p>
      <p>CWI is a real answer to that: hands-on training for in-demand careers, at a price that makes a living possible without the debt. The barrier was never tuition or schedules. It was the decision itself.</p>
      <p>So the job is to make something people write off as unsexy feel worth wanting. Real cuts, framing, and motion that show what it actually looks like to get hands-on inside a program, until a two-year degree looks like somewhere you want to be.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="paper eg">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eg-head rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ The system</span>
      <h2>DJ built the guide the whole campaign edits <span class="serif">to.</span></h2>
      <!-- DJ 2026-07-14: "i built this along the way, not before it got cut. show
           developing with the campaign." The old line claimed the guide was written
           BEFORE the first spot, which is backwards. COPY BELOW IS CLAUDE'S DRAFT - DJ
           to approve or rewrite in his own words. -->
      <p class="eg-sub">The guide came out of the work, not ahead of it. Round by round DJ wrote down what was working: the type, the color, the pacing, the export specs. It grew as the campaign grew, and every editor on every round cuts to the current version, so four years of films still read as one thing across every program and every screen.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="eg-grid rv">
      {[1,2,3,4,5,6].map((n) => (
        <figure class="eg-shot"><img src={`/case-studies/cwi/editguide/eg-${n}.png`} alt={`CWI video style guide, page ${n}`} loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
      ))}
    </div>
