<section class="paper">
  <div class="wrap story">
    <div class="side rv">
      <span class="k mono">\ DJ's part</span>
      <h2>DJ directs it, runs the set, and <span class="serif">cuts it.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body rv">
      <!-- DJ 2026-07-14: "I direct (I dont shoot these) I just do on set." Every claim that
           he shoots these spots is gone: the DPs are Jake Rapp, Nathan Zanders and Kova
           Kovatonic, and Vision Kit shoots the stills. He directs, runs the set, and cuts. -->
      <p>DJ directs and cuts the Let's Get Started program spots, working alongside the agency Against, executive producer Steph Norrell and producer Tess Rizvi, with Jake Rapp, Nathan Zanders and Kova Kovatonic on camera and Vision Kit on stills. Every quarter we make four to six new films with a crew of five to twenty, and DJ builds each one around the specific program, digging into what that path actually gives a student.</p>
      <p>Real students play the leads. On shoot days DJ runs the set: directing the talent, working with the DP on how it gets shot, and keeping the crew moving with Tess on production, then he takes it into the edit and cuts it for every screen. He frames the students as the heroes and puts the real tools and payoff of the program on screen.</p>
      <p>DJ has worked in Idaho education for more than ten years, and he brings that to every round. This one is homegrown, made with hometown friends and a client as fired up about it as he is. Together we're putting Idaho opportunities in front of the students who benefit most, and shifting the culture a little each quarter.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

